ion() {\n      const button = document.getElementById('jokeBtn');\n      const jokeDisplay = document.getElementById('joke');\n\n      if (button) {\n        button.addEventListener('click', function () {\n           const joke = jokes[Math.floor(Math.random() * 4)];\n           jokeDisplay.textContent = joke;\n        });\n      }\n    </script>\n</body>\n</html>\n```\n\n**How it works**\n\n1. The List `jokes` holds the 4 jokes.  \n2. The `<button>` listener adds a `click` event to the button.  \n3. When the button is clicked, we use `Math.random()` to pick a random index from the jokes array (0-4).  \n4. The result shows the joke in the `<div id=\"joke\"></div>`.\n\nFeel free to tweak the jokes, styling or the button label to match your taste. Enjoy!",
